Fork-local patch, not part of radxa-pkg's debian/patches series.

get_fw_path() copies a non-empty aic_fw_path override with memcpy of
strlen() bytes, so the result is never NUL-terminated. The callers added
by fix-sdio-per-chip-firmware-path pass uninitialised FW_PATH_MAX stack
buffers and then format them with %s, reading past the copied path.
Bound and terminate the copy the same way the default branch already does.

This system builds only the USB driver, not the SDIO tree; the fix keeps
the applied series correct anyway.

--- a/src/SDIO/driver_fw/driver/aic8800/aic8800_bsp/aicsdio.c
+++ b/src/SDIO/driver_fw/driver/aic8800/aic8800_bsp/aicsdio.c
@@ -2091,7 +2091,7 @@
 
 void get_fw_path(char* fw_path){
 	if (strlen(aic_fw_path) > 0) {
-		memcpy(fw_path, aic_fw_path, strlen(aic_fw_path));
+		snprintf(fw_path, FW_PATH_MAX, "%s", aic_fw_path);
 	}else{
 		snprintf(fw_path, FW_PATH_MAX, "%s%s", aic_default_fw_path, aicbsp_chip_fw_subdir());
 	}
